    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0575" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1818</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-13T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>180. Your 134, April 30, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d591-f1"/> received May 18,
                    7 p.m., and 205, May 26.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d591-f2"/></p>
                <p>After consulting Secretary of Navy suggest you get in touch with Captain Bierer,
                    commander of <hi rendition="#italic">Olympia</hi>, who is under direct orders of
                    the British Admiral at Murmansk. No additional American cruiser at present
                    available to Murman coast or White Sea. Department studying question and will
                    advise if anything further is possible but no further measures contemplated for
                    the present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
